/**
\mainpage microlab500 EPICS Support Module
\section intro_sec Introduction
This is an EPICS support module for the Hamilton Microlab 500 series syringe pumps. It currently supports a single controller on a serial line. Communication uses streamDevice, so an Asyn port is required.

<a href="http://www.microlabtech.co.uk/documents/literature/ML%20500%20B-C%20Manual.pdf">The instrument user manual is available here. </a> 

\section macros_sec Macros
Macros used in the templates:

- P: Device prefix
- R: Device suffix
- PORT: Name of the Asyn Port for communication with device
- STROKESIZE: Number of steps per full syringe stroke. Default configuration is 1000 (half resolution mode) - please see manual Appendix F, p. F-19.
- LEFTSYRINGEVOL: Volume in microliters of the left syringe
- RIGHTSYRINGEVOL: Volume in microliters of the right syringe

\section user_sec Interface 
The instrument has two sides, each composed of a valve and a syringe drive.
Each valve is represented by an mbbo record and each syringe drive is represented by a motor record. In the record names below, \$(SIDE) is either LEFT or RIGHT.

<table>
    <tr>
        <td><b>\$(P)\$(R):\$(SIDE):SETVPOS</b> </td> 
        <td>
            An mbbo record to set the valve position. Choices:

            - 0: Input
            - 1: Wash
            - 2: Output

        </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><b>\$(P)\$(R):\$(SIDE):MOTOR</b> </td>
        <td>
            A motor record representing the syringve. Engineering units are microliters.
            The motor resolution and soft limits are controlled by the LEFTSYRINGEVOL and RIGHTSYRINGEVOL macros.
            Due to a limitation of the serial protocol, the STOP field of either motor record will stop all motion
            on the controller, not only the chosen syringe.
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

In addition certain functions can be accessed directly via their own records:

<table>
    <tr>
        <td><b>\$(P)\$(R):\$(SIDE):GETVPOS</b> </td>
        <td>
            Read back valve position.
            
            - 0: Input
            - 1: Wash
            - 2: Output

        </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><b>\$(P)\$(R):\$(SIDE):PICKUP</b> </td>
        <td>
            Cause the syringe to pick up by the number of steps stored in \$(P)\$(R):\$(SIDE):STEP

        </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><b>\$(P)\$(R):\$(SIDE):DISPENSE</b> </td>
        <td>
            Cause the syringe to dispense by the number of steps stored in \$(P)\$(R):\$(SIDE):STEP

        </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><b>\$(P)\$(R):\$(SIDE):SETSPEED</b> </td>
        <td>
            Set the syringe speed in the controller's raw units of seconds per full syringe stroke.

        </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><b>\$(P)\$(R):\$(SIDE):SETRETURN</b> </td>
        <td>
            Set the number of backoff return steps.

        </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><b>\$(P)\$(R):STOP</b> </td>
        <td>
            Stop all motion on this controller.

        </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><b>\$(P)\$(R):STARTUP</b> </td>
        <td>
            Perform all actions required after pump is connected or after IOC is resterted. Executed once when IOC starts.

        </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><b>\$(P)\$(R):INITIALISE</b> </td>
        <td>
            Perform pump initialisation routine. Required after pump is powered on. This includes homing the syringes so all parts of the pump will move. 

        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

\section starting_sec Getting started

- Choose a terminal server port. Set up an AsynIP port to point to this terminal server port, and put the AsynIP port name in the PORT macro of the microlab500 template.
- Power on the pump and connect its RS232 cable.
- The pump's own control panel RS232 cable should not be connected, otherwise communication is not possible.
- Start the IOC
- Press Connect on the GUI - executes \$(P)\$(R):STARTUP
- Press Initialise on GUI - executes \$(P)\$(R):INITIALISE.

If RS232 connection is lost:
    
- Reconnect the RS232 cable
- Press Connect on the GUI

If the pump is powered off

- Power the pump on
- Press Connect on the GUI
- Press Initialise on the GUI - caution, the pump will move

If the IOC is restarted

- Connect is executed automatically when the IOC starts, so if the pump is powered on and connected, communications will be re-established.

\section build_sec Build Instructions 
- \subpage build_instructions_example

IOCs build using these build instructions are available in iocs/

\section iocs_sec Example IOCs

Two sample IOCs are provided, <i>example</i> and <i>example_s2</i>. Example runs with the hardware while example_s2 runs with a basic simulator. The simulator is located in etc/simulations/microlab500_sim.py. 

Both IOCs have a sample EDM screen which gives access to all the basic commands and a standard motor record embedded screen for each side of the instrument. Build and run the <i>example</i> IOC, and start its GUI with the following commands:

<pre>
cd iocs/example
make
./bin/linux-x86_64/stexample.sh
./bin/linux-x86_64/stexample-gui
</pre>

**/

